  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention unfavorable outcomes, probabilities of zero, or asymmetry in the distribution. Instead, the justification is based solely on the certainty of the outcome in A. The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness—specifically, whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes—and preferring the more right-skewed lottery. Since the individual does not consider this aspect and instead relies on certainty, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s justification does not reflect the rule of the decision reason (preference for more right-skewed lotteries). Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
